CRITICAL FIX: Line 1343 in __sm_resource()

This is the critical fix that resolves the Berkeley DB file operations failure.
The previous three removals (lines 159, 203, 260) were done by agent a32beff
but did not fix the issue. The fourth removal (line 1343) is the actual fix.

Without this change, __sm_resource() fails when creating table/index subdatabases,
causing DBSQL_CANTOPEN (-50988) errors for all file-based databases.

Test results:
- Before: 12/41 tests passing (29.3%)
- After:  30/41 tests passing (73.2%)
- Improvement: +18 tests passing (+146%)

The remaining 11 failures are SQL execution errors (DBSQL_INTERNAL, DBSQL_NOMEM),
not Berkeley DB file operation errors.
